"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":680,"closed_issues":22796,"state":"open","created_at":"2018-01-18T16:52:20Z","updated_at":"2026-03-11T06:25:22Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":9,"created_at":"2017-04-28T11:44:26Z","updated_at":"2019-09-13T08:21:29Z","closed_at":"2018-02-18T21:27:50Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Edit (vicb) - the error is caused by the ngIf\r\n\r\n```html        \r\n<p *ngIf=\"user.removed; else activeBlock\">User had been removed: {{user.removed | date : 'dd.MM.yyyy'}}</p>\r\n<p #activeBlock>User is active</p>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe second `<p>` should be a `<ng-template>` but the error message does not help\r\n\r\nHi.\r\nProbably i found an error.\r\n\r\nI've used **ngIf block** inside **ngFor block** also inside **ngFor block** placed another **ngFor**.\r\n\r\nLike this:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<tr *ngFor=\"let user of users\">\r\n    <td>\r\n        <p *ngFor=\"let login of users.logins\">{{login}}</p>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td>\r\n        <p *ngIf=\"user.removed; else activeBlock\">User had been removed: {{user.removed | date : 'dd.MM.yyyy'}}</p>\r\n        <p #activeBlock>User is active</p>\r\n    </td>\r\n</tr>\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd this throws error: **templateRef.createEmbeddedView is not a function**\r\n\r\nI'm using this code now (instead previous):\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<tr *ngFor=\"let user of users\">\r\n    <td>\r\n        <p *ngFor=\"let login of users.logins\">{{login}}</p>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td>\r\n        <p *ngIf=\"user.removed\">User had been removed: {{user.removed | date : 'dd.MM.yyyy'}}</p>\r\n        <p  *ngIf=\"!user.removed\">User is active</p>\r\n    </td>\r\n</tr>\r\n```\r\nThanks for attention.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"vicb","id":248818,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODgxOA==","avatar_url":"https: